course: dictionary
lesson: 13405
title: Formal words: herein
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Herein is a formal word. It means "in this document" or "in here", and you will find it in official papers, legal letters and rules. Most people do not use it in everyday talk.
explain: «Please read the terms herein before you sign the form.» Look at the words around herein: terms, sign, form. These are clues that you are reading a paper. Herein points to that paper, so the terms are written inside the form itself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. Does «Please read the terms in this document before you sign the form» still make sense? If it does, you have worked out the meaning of herein.
fact: Herein is an adverb, and it means in this document or in here.
fact: Herein is formal, so you will mostly see it in legal papers, official letters and formal writing.
fact: Herein is often used with contained, as in «the information contained herein», which means the information inside this document.
fact: «Herein» means in this document, so «the rules herein» means the rules written in this paper.
fact: In everyday talk, say "in this" or "in here" instead of herein.
exercise: «Please read the rules herein before you start.» What does herein mean? | Very quickly | Outside the school gate | *In this document | Long ago
exercise: «All the facts contained herein are true.» Where are the facts? | In the playground | In a river | *In this document | Under the table
exercise: «The form is long, but the answers are all herein.» Copy the word that means in this document. | long | *herein | answers | form
test: «Herein lies the answer to the puzzle.» What does herein mean in this sentence? | *In this place or document | Very sad and quiet | Ready to go out | Far away over the sea
test: A lawyer writes, «The notes are kept herein.» Which word could replace herein with the same meaning? | *In this document | Yonder | Upstairs | Nearby
exam: «The terms herein are important.» What is the best meaning of herein? | *Written in this document | Painted on a wall | Lost forever | Shouted loudly
